    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0203" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg179"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Nelson.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 63.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 19, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>Your despatches to 124 inclusive have been
                    received.</p>
                <p>I have to express my cordial approval of your course in the pending controversy
                    between Chili and Bolivia, which I trust is still within the reach of a peaceful
                    and honorable settlement.</p>
                <p>The Senate having by resolution called for information on the subject, a copy of
                    your No. 123 and of its enclosures has been communicated to that body by the
                    President.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas H. Nelson</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
